# 11. REFERRAL AND AFFILIATE PROGRAMME

This is a major feature of PROXY AI.

Build a complete referral programme that allows members to earn commission by inviting new paying members.

The platform owner must also earn from the referral programme through retained subscription revenue.

## A. Unique referral links

Every member receives a unique referral code.

Example:

proxyai.com/register?ref=PROXY123

When a new person registers through the link:
- Record the referral code.
- Identify the referring member.
- Link the new account to the referrer.
- Record the registration date.
- Track subsequent subscription purchases.
- Track subscription renewals.

Preserve referral attribution throughout the registration and payment process.

Use a configurable attribution window, initially 90 days.

## B. Referral commission

Set the default referral commission at:

**10% of eligible subscription revenue.**

Example:

A referred member purchases a $5 Pro Worker subscription.

| Description | Amount |
|---|---:|
| Subscription payment | $5.00 |
| Referrer commission (10%) | $0.50 |
| PROXY AI retained revenue | $4.50 |

For an $8 Top-Rated subscription:

| Description | Amount |
|---|---:|
| Subscription payment | $8.00 |
| Referrer commission (10%) | $0.80 |
| PROXY AI retained revenue | $7.20 |

These examples exclude applicable operating expenses, taxes, payment-processing fees and refunds.

## C. Recurring referral commissions

Referral commission should apply to:
- First eligible subscription payment.
- Eligible quarterly renewals.
- Eligible membership upgrades.

For example, when a referred member renews their $5 subscription, the referrer earns another $0.50.

Calculate commissions only after successful payment confirmation.

Do not calculate commissions on:
- Failed payments.
- Cancelled transactions.
- Unpaid invoices.
- Refunded payments.
- Chargebacks.

Reverse previously credited commissions when an eligible payment is refunded or charged back.

